<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26952" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικλίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλίνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>double-folding,</i> epith. of
			doors or gates, mostly in pl. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σανίδες,
				θύραι, πύλαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.345
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.268
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.455
			</span></i>; later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικλίδες</span> alone,
				<i>folding-doors,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				7.182
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				5.144
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Asclep.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				255
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.), etc.: rarely in sg., <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				14.42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.241
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Eratosth.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. θύρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					193
				</span></i>
			:—written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκλεις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ειδος</span>, as if from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλείς,</span>
			<i>double-fastened,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				7
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i> ad loc.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
